Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: add ESPN odds + BPI 4th agent to multi-agent
 analysis
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- scripts/fetch_odds.py: pulls DraftKings spread/moneylines, ESPN BPI
  win probability, line movement (open→close), and futures (regional +
  championship implied probability) for all tournament games via ESPN
  hidden API — no external API key required

- api/analyze.js: adds odds_agent as 4th parallel LangGraph node
  * loads espn_odds.json in getData() with graceful fallback
  * routerNode builds odds_data context string per matchup:
    spread, O/U, implied win %, BPI win %, matchup quality,
    line movement direction, futures championship odds
  * odds_agent interprets market + BPI, uses market-implied prob
    as baseline, BPI as second model
  * synthesis weights updated: efficiency 40%, market/BPI 20%,
    form 20%, matchup 20% (degrades to 50/25/25 if no odds data)
  * synthesis now flags market/model divergence >8 pts explicitly

- .github/workflows/refresh.yml: runs fetch_odds.py after fetch_data.py,
  copies espn_odds.json to public/data on every daily refresh

- data/espn_odds.json, public/data/espn_odds.json: seeded empty so
  analyze.js gracefully degrades before first odds fetch run
