Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: fetch full regular season + postseason data (was
 returning tournament only)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: ESPN schedule endpoint without explicit seasontype param defaults
to the currently active season type. During March Madness that returns only
postseason (type 3) — dropping the entire regular season.

Fix: fetch_data.py now makes two explicit requests per team:
  ?season=2026&seasontype=2  (regular season, ~34 games/team)
  ?season=2026&seasontype=3  (postseason: conf tourney + NCAA tournament)
Results are merged and deduplicated before processing.

Before fix: 58 total games, 44 inter-bracket edges (tournament only)
After fix:  2046 total games, 444 inter-bracket edges (full season)

Transitive analysis recomputed with full data:
  2495 not-played pairs analyzed, 655 pairs with 3+ signals (was near zero)

All data files rebuilt and copied to public/data.
